# Coil — Debug and automation surface

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
Coil carries a small debugging and automation surface, `window.__coil`, so the
game can be driven and inspected from code without pressing a key or waiting on
real time.

You implement it. Every operation this file specifies is a deliverable, and the
build installs the finished surface on `window.__coil` as soon as the game has
initialized. Every scenario driven from code reaches the game through it, so it
is present and exactly as specified here.

Each operation is a read of the game's state or a pose of one part of it. A pose
sets one thing, and the game's own tick, turning, collision, pellet placement,
and scoring run from there exactly as they do in play, so a scenario driven from
code behaves exactly like one played by hand.

The surface is inert during normal play, doing nothing until something calls it.
{{else if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
Coil carries a small debugging and automation surface so the game can be driven
